{"type":"message","id":"ea31bed4","parentId":"f1ceb8c8","timestamp":"2026-04-02T11:30:55.849Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_wpoqcuqu2puc_1","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"OpenClaw 2026.4.1 changelog release notes\",\n  \"provider\": \"duckduckgo\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 958,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"duckduckgo\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5dee3aade56c50e9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nReleases · openclaw/openclaw - GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5dee3aade56c50e9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/releases\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"adc5ada559e53e71\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nACP/ACPX agent registry: align OpenClaw's ACPX built-in agent mirror with the latest openclaw /acpx command defaults and built-in aliases, pin versioned npx built-ins to exact versions, and stop unknown ACP agent ids from falling through to raw --agent command execution on the MCP-proxy path. (#28321) Thanks @m0nkmaster and @vincentkoc.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"adc5ada559e53e71\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"github.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5da5cb03e64bf115\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChangelog — What's New in OpenClaw Desktop\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5da5cb03e64bf115\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openclawdesktop.com/changelog.html\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6081b87a7aa3d606\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRelease Notes What's New in OpenClaw Desktop Every feature, fix, and milestone — newest first.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6081b87a7aa3d606\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"openclawdesktop.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a5f271c9d52e74b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOpenClaw 2026.4.1 Release: GLM 5.1 Integration, AWS Bedrock Guardrails ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a5f271c9d52e74b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://blockchain.news/ainews/openclaw-2026-4-1-release-glm-5-1-integration-aws-bedrock-guardrails-and-40-stability-fixes-practical-ai-agent-upgrade-analysis\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"81f2e06ae0d44d28\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAccording to @ openclaw on X, the OpenClaw 2026.4.1 release adds GLM 5.1 support with a non-looping failover mechanism, AWS Bedrock Guardrails integration, a /tasks feature for agent task logging, per-job cron tool allowlists, and 40+ stability and execution fixes, with details published in the project's GitHub release notes . As reported by the OpenClaw GitHub release page, the GLM 5.1 ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"81f2e06ae0d44d28\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"blockchain.news\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1ea484be4c731abc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOpenClaw Latest Version — Current Release & Changelog | DeployClaw\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1ea484be4c731abc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://deployclaw.com/tools/openclaw-latest-version\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"976b5861f26bd330\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCheck the latest OpenClaw release version, view changelog , download links, and installation instructions. Always stay up to date with the newest OpenClaw release .\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"976b5861f26bd330\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"deployclaw.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b39a44645649dffe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nComparing v2026.4.1...main · openclaw/openclaw · GitHub\\