{"type":"message","id":"9d620f75","parentId":"ea31bed4","timestamp":"2026-04-02T11:30:55.899Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_wpoqcuqu2puc_2","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"OpenClaw 2026.3.28 changelog\",\n  \"provider\": \"duckduckgo\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1009,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"duckduckgo\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"71119b1425debae9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nReleases · openclaw/openclaw - GitHub\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"71119b1425debae9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/releases\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d56ea84dd2cafd5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2026.3.28-beta.1 Breaking Providers/Qwen: remove the deprecated qwen-portal-auth OAuth integration for portal.qwen.ai; migrate to Model Studio with openclaw onboard --auth-choice modelstudio-api-key. (#52709) Thanks @pomelo-nwu. Config/Doctor: drop automatic config migrations older than two months; very old legacy keys now fail validation instead of being rewritten on load or by openclaw ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d56ea84dd2cafd5\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"github.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fba7d7cd2e874bba\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nopenclaw/openclaw v2026.3.28 on GitHub - NewReleases.io\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fba7d7cd2e874bba\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://newreleases.io/project/github/openclaw/openclaw/release/v2026.3.28\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57d2cbf066e68e7a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNew release openclaw / openclaw version v2026.3.28 openclaw 2026.3.28 on GitHub.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57d2cbf066e68e7a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"newreleases.io\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4605af5074fb541c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOpenClaw 2026.3.28: Approval Gates for Tool Calls and Built-In xAI ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4605af5074fb541c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.clawly.org/news/openclaw-2026328-approval-gates-for-tool-calls-and-built-in-xai-search\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fab48f79eb7b3858\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOpenClaw 2026.3.28 introduced a set of changes that matter for people running self-hosted/personal agents in production. What changed (and why it matters) 1) Approval gates can now happen before a tool call runs The release adds async approval hooks for tool execution. In practice, this gives you a stronger safety checkpoint for high-risk actions (shell, network writes, external sends) before ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fab48f79eb7b3858\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.clawly.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"52463763c8b20570\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOpenClaw 2026.3.28 Update: What's New + Critical Security Patches\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"52463763c8b20570\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://blink.new/blog/openclaw-2026-3-28-whats-new-update-guide\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"24a388baa2c1ca1a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOpenClaw 2026.3.28 update brings plug-in approval hooks, xAI Grok integration, and patches two critical CVEs. Here's what changed and why you must update now.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"24a388baa2c1ca1a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"blink.new\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a0076ef0f04d3f3e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUpdate News: OpenClaw 2026.3.28 Just Dropped\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a0076ef0f04d3f3e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://aimiockto.substack.com/p/update-news-openclaw-2026328-just\",\n      \"snippet\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"32498d27c4467014\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe OpenClaw team shipped 2026.3.28 this morning, and there's enough here to warrant a proper breakdown. Let's dig in.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"32498d27c4467014\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"aimiockto.substack.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"OpenClaw 2026.3.28 changelog","provider":"duckduckgo","count":5,"tookMs":1009,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"duckduckgo","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"71119b1425debae9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nReleases · openclaw/openclaw - GitHub\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"71119b1425debae9\">>>","url":"https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/releases","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0d56ea84dd2cafd5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2026.3.28-beta.1 Breaking Providers/Qwen: remove the deprecated qwen-portal-auth OAuth integration for portal.qwen.ai; migrate to Model Studio with openclaw onboard --auth-choice modelstudio-api-key. (#52709) Thanks @pomelo-nwu. Config/Doctor: drop automatic config migrations older than two months; very old legacy keys now fail validation instead of being rewritten on load or by openclaw ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0d56ea84dd2cafd5\">>>","siteName":"github.com"},{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fba7d7cd2e874bba\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nopenclaw/openclaw v2026.3.28 on GitHub - NewReleases.io\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"fba7d7cd2e874bba\">>>","url":"https://newreleases.io/project/github/openclaw/openclaw/release/v2026.3.28","snippet":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57d2cbf066e68e7a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNew release openclaw / openclaw version v202